#v(1em)

Dear Wolfgang,

I am applying for the Developer position for Kubernetes-based Cloud Services for AI-enabled Observability in SAP BTP. The role is listed at T2, and I want to be upfront that I would be joining at T1.

I will be honest: Kubernetes and Go are not in my current stack. What draws me to this role is the AI enablement angle. I follow the space closely, build with AI workflows in my own time, and have hands-on experience with agentic coding and LLM systems. For a university project I built a moderation system combining a fine-tuned XLM-RoBERTa classifier with an LLM-as-a-Judge layer, which gave me a concrete understanding of how AI components need to be designed for reliability at scale.

On the infrastructure side, Docker is part of how I work daily, and I am comfortable in Linux environments. I am aware that Kubernetes is a steep learning curve, but I am the kind of developer who learns fastest by being close to production systems.

I finish my dual studies in Business Informatics at DHBW Mannheim in September 2026 and hold an unconditional hire recommendation from SAP. I would be glad to talk about where I could contribute and where I would need to grow.

#v(2em)

Best regards,

#v(0.5em)

*Max Meinel*
